 A non-zero exit means the service is down. Fail fast and report it, because a retry cannot help.
 
+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "Call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exited 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is it a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Is it a timeout, 502, 503 or 504?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Retry up to 3 times, same key, after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and report" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "Call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exited 0?";
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no, service down"];
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Is it a POST?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST?" -> "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST?" -> "Is it a timeout, 502, 503 or 504?" [label="no"];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report";
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Is it a timeout, 502, 503 or 504?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a timeout, 502, 503 or 504?" -> "Retry up to 3 times, same key, after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a timeout, 502, 503 or 504?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no, fix the request"];
+}
+```
+
+The key check comes before the status check. A timeout or a 503 on a keyless POST still means fail fast.
+
